# Playtest report — Snake build to play #1 (release `play-1`)

**Build played:** `snake-build-1.zip` from release `play-1` in `world/producer` (game-developer 78f16e43, artist f5b3b5d5), unzipped and served statically (`python3 -m http.server`) at `/index.html`.
**How:** headless Chromium (Playwright 1.64), 1280×800 viewport, real keyboard/mouse events, real-time play at the build's normal pace (130 ms/tick). A bot pressing real arrow keys steered to food; game state was read from `window.__snake` only to decide moves and to report. Scripts: `play.py`, `self2.py`. Recording: `play-1-session.webm`. Screenshots: `shots/`.
Limits: no human hands/ears; sound was checked only as files (3 short wavs, 0.14–0.6 s, peaks −3 dB, no clipping) — I did not listen to them in a browser.

## Per requirement
| Req | Result | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| R1 runs in browser, no build step | PASS | loads from static server, no console errors/warnings across the whole run (title → play → eat → die → replay ×3) |
| R2 grid, steady pace | PASS | 20×20 checker board, snake moves cell by cell; interval 130 ms at score 0 (`04-play-score.png`) |
| R3 arrow keys / reverse / scroll | PASS | Left while heading right: ignored, still alive (head kept advancing). `scrollY` stayed 0; at 800×600 the page is exactly viewport-height (no scrollbar) |
| R4 food | PASS | scores 1,2,3…6 with length 4,5,6…9 (exactly +1/+1 each); food respawns on a free cell (`03-ate-first.png`, `04-play-score.png`) |
| R5 death | PASS | wall death (`06-gameover-wall.png`, cause=wall) and self death (`08-gameover-self.png`, cause=self, via real keys down/left/up at 135 ms spacing on a 6-long snake) |
| R6 title | PASS | `01-title.png`: "SNAKE", rules line, "Arrow keys to turn", "Press Enter or Space to start"; an arrow key also starts the game |
